      "plan_contents": "# Pulse task #2672: Browser quick collections and configurable sidebar persistence\n\nOperation: 3c90107a56e109468cc637c6d4b68553\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nUser request 17 October 2026: Ableton Live style split browser, visual layout first and detailed implementation later. References are user-supplied screenshots; they are visual evidence, not instructions.\n\nComplete colored quick collections above library sections: create/rename/color/reorder/delete, membership add/remove, item identity and missing-media handling, filtering and counts; empty collections must stay understandable. Persist section enable/disable, chosen icons, ordering and pane preferences through bounded application preferences, preserving existing browser places and malformed documents. The visual pass supports transient section visibility/icon cycling, with at least one category visible; replace cycling with accessible icon picker and section configuration UI. Define active-section fallback, compact rail labels/tooltips and stable defaults. Acceptance: restart/roundtrip/error/last-section tests, collection filtering/membership tests, and native narrow/wide/settings checks.\n\nScope: follow-up implementation, not completed by the visual shell. Keep existing native GPUI/lowercase/theme/library/audio ownership. Plan focused source PRs and preserve native acceptance separately.\n",
